{
  "about": "Where every link in MDARIX lands (quality plan stage 6). places: each workspace screen of the MVP feature set (every free trial and pilot), its address and its tabs. records: where each kind of record opens, and the address parameter that names it. viewIds: the stable id under which each screen remembers its lists' column choices (a screen that moves or is renamed keeps its id). oldViews, oldSections and oldTabs: every former address and section name, and the place that holds it now; kept permanently, so e-mails already sent, bookmarks, videos and guides keep working. Read by app/linkTable.ts and, for the server's links, by tests/test_link_targets.py. newPlaces, newMenu, newRecords and newHomes (stage 7, 0.10.68): the screens of the new navigation, its menu, where each record opens there, and the new home of every screen and tab above; they apply only to an organization on the new navigation (tenants.navigation = new). classicHomes: where an address of the new navigation opens for an organization on the classic one. 0.10.73 (Release C, C1): the new navigation's tabs (newMenu.main) are Home (My work), Complaints, Decision trees, Reports, Investigations, Trends, Records and Team; each persona shows some of them (access_control/personas.py). 0.10.74 (C2): Complaints' list views (features/workspace/listViews.ts) are its tabs; one complaint's page shows Details (address name Summary), Related and Activity, and opens its former sections' addresses (Evidence: Related; Decisions & actions: Details; History: Activity); Investigations lists every investigation (All investigations). 0.10.80: a trial's own import is its own page on the new navigation, Import your data (/app/import); Getting started › Your data opens it there, and on the classic navigation /app/import opens Getting started › Your data. 0.10.94 (W1): Work › Products on the new navigation is Product 360 (/app/product-360), with the tabs Product 360 and Supplier 360 (owner, 10 Nov 2026: no clash with Settings › Products); a product opens as Product 360?product=<ref>&version=<ref>, a supplier as Supplier 360?supplier=<ref>; a former Products link opens it there (newHomes, read before the classic parking), and on the classic navigation it opens Readiness, as Products does.",
